Happy to help you get started 🙏

Here's a simple way to begin — just two scriptures:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (Ta Pei Chou)** — 3 times a day
Before reciting, say:
*"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [say your full name], grant me good health and a peaceful mind."*

📿 **Heart Sutra (Hsin Ching)** — 3 times a day
Before reciting, say:
*"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [say your full name], grant me wisdom and relieve my worries."*

⚠️ Please avoid reciting the Heart Sutra after 10PM, or during thunderstorms.

If you don't know how to pronounce the words, don't worry — you can follow along with the guided videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Start with these two. Once you're comfortable with them, we can add the **Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance (Li Fo Ta Chan Hui Wen)** — that's the third pillar of the practice.

One thing that will help me guide you better:

**Have you recited any Buddhist scriptures before, or is this completely new to you?**

