Q: I have severe insomnia, which sutras should I recite?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,qa_general,qa_metaphysics
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Not being able to sleep wears a person down — I understand 🙏

You can start with these two:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (Da Bei Zhou)** — 3 times daily
Before reciting, say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me good health, safety and peace of mind"*

📿 **Heart Sutra (Xin Jing)** — 3 times daily
Before reciting, say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom, a clear and calm mind, and free me from afflictions"*
⚠️ Do not recite the Heart Sutra after 10pm — best in the daytime, especially if you're feeling weak. Recite it earlier in the day, not right before bed.

Master Lu's standard daily practice is the Great Compassion Mantra 7 times and the Heart Sutra 7 times, with the Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance as the third pillar added once these two feel natural — but start small and keep it steady. Consistency matters more than volume.

If you don't know the pronunciation, there are chant-along videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

May I ask — have you recited sutras before, or is this completely new to you? That helps me know where to take it next 🙏

═══ CHIP2-en I keep arguing wit — guard: clean ═══
Q: I keep arguing with family, what can I start learning?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 1 (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: introduction,qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Arguing with the people closest to us is one of the most draining kinds of pain 🙏

Master Lu explained it this way in *Buddhism Q&A*:

> To a certain extent, interpersonal conflicts are the results of karmic conflicts from your previous lives.

So the method isn't to win the argument — it's to dissolve the knot behind it.

You can start here:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 times a day
Before reciting, say: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], with good health and strengthened energy."

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 3 times a day
Before reciting, say: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], to gain wisdom, keep a clear and calm mind, and remove my worries."
(Please don't recite the Heart Sutra after 10pm.)

📿 **Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots** — 21 times a day
Before reciting, say: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me, [your full name], and [family member's full name] to resolve our negative karmic ties."

If you're not sure how to pronounce them, there are chant-along videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Master Lu also taught that you can recite the **Heart Sutra** for the family member themselves, asking Guan Yin Bodhisattva to bless them and grant them wisdom — it's best not to tell them you're doing it.

Just keep going. As your own mind settles, the atmosphere at home usually changes before the other person does 🙏

One question so I can point you better: **have you recited sutras before, or is this completely new to you?**

Reference: *Buddhism Q&A* (Q116), *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 1* (Q006), *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3* (Q116)

═══ CHIP3-en Work has been goin — guard: passed_after_retry ═══
Q: Work has been going badly, is it karma?
Sources: Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 1 (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: qa_general,qa_metaphysics,introduction
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
