  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Work troubles wear a person down — I understand 🙏

Master Lu did teach that our outer circumstances are connected to our karma. In *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 2*, when explaining negative karma, he said:

> The more black energy patches there are on the body, the more unpleasant experiences with health, career and relationships this person would be having.

But the more important part of his teaching is this — it can be changed. In the *Introduction to the Guan Yin Citta Dharma Door*, Master Lu said:

> For true Buddhists who are learning and practising Buddhism, I would like tell all of you: our fate and fortune are within our own control.

So the answer isn't to accept a bad patch — it's to start clearing it.

You can begin with:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 times daily
Before reciting say: "May Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], with good health and strengthen my spiritual energy."

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 3 times daily
Before reciting say: "May Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], to open my wisdom, to have a clear and calm mind, and to remove my worries."
⚠️ Not to be recited after 10pm.

📿 **Cundi Mantra** — 21 times daily (for career matters)
Before reciting say: "May Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], that my wishes be fulfilled and my work goes smoothly."

If you're not sure of the pronunciation, you can chant along with the teaching videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Keep it up steadily — the Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance (for repenting and eliminating karmic obstacles) is the third pillar, best added once these become comfortable, starting from 1 time a day.

May I ask — have you chanted before, or is this new to you? That helps me point you to the right starting place 🙏

═══ CHIP4-en My child is rebell — guard: clean ═══
Q: My child is rebellious, how should I handle my emotions?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ scoped 没有写明遍数 line (info only)
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
This is one of the hardest kinds of pain — you love the child, and the love keeps getting turned into anger 🙏

Master Lu's teaching on this is very direct:

> First, you should not use an adult's way of thinking to restrain the innocent and playful nature of children.

And on why the friction feels so personal:

> If a child is having conflicts with their parents or family members, it may be due to karmic conflicts from previous lives, or the child may have come to collect karmic debts from the parents. Therefore, you need to recite the Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots.

So the work isn't mainly on the child's behaviour — it's on the karmic knot between you two, and on your own mind staying clear.

You can start with this:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 times a day
Prayer: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], with good health and strengthened spiritual energy"

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 3 times a day (for yourself — this is the one for your emotions)
Prayer: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], to gain wisdom, keep a clear and calm mind, and remove my worries"
⚠️ Not after 10pm

📿 **Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots** — 21 times a day
Prayer: "May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me, [your full name], and [child's full name], resolve our negative karmic ties"

You can also recite **Heart Sutra** separately for the child, praying for Guan Yin Bodhisattva to grant him/her wisdom.

One caution from Master Lu that many parents don't know — for a child who is hard to discipline, **keep the Great Compassion Mantra you recite for them to no more than 7 times per day**. Reciting a lot of it for a misbehaved child can increase their spiritual energy and make them even harder to handle.

Keep going steadily. As your own mind settles, the house usually settles with it 🙏

Can I ask one thing — have you chanted before, or is this new to you? It changes where I'd suggest you start.

Reference: *Buddhism Q&A* (Q127), *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3* (Q114)

═══ CHIP5-en I am new to 心灵法门,  — guard: clean ═══
Q: I am new to 心灵法门, what is the first step?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,qa_metaphysics
