  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Welcome 🙏 Starting is simpler than most people expect.

You can begin today with just two:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (Ta Pei Chou)** — 3 times a day
Before reciting, say: *"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me good health."*

📿 **Heart Sutra (Hsin Ching)** — 3 times a day
Before reciting, say: *"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom and remove my worries."*
⚠️ Please avoid reciting the Heart Sutra after 10PM.

If you don't know how to pronounce the words, don't worry — follow along with the teaching videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen

Once these two feel comfortable to you, we can add the third pillar, the **Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance (Li Fo Ta Chan Hui Wen)** — that one starts at just 1 time a day, and also not after 10PM.

Master Lu explained in the *Introduction to the Guan Yin Citta Dharma Door*:

> Performing Daily Recitation is as important as daily food intakes, and it is like earning an income for daily living expenses.

So daily consistency matters much more than large numbers.

May I ask — have you recited any sutras before, or is this completely new to you? That helps me point you to the right starting point 🙏

Reference: *Introduction to the Guan Yin Citta Dharma Door*, p.10, 11

═══ CHIP6-en My family member i — guard: clean ═══
Q: My family member is ill, what should I recite for them?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
